      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The AI correctly spotted the conflict (someone can’t die in 1861 and get married in 1870). But it also added its own inference that the researcher had confirmed the death record was for the right person, when the researcher never actually said that. That extra assumption wasn’t in the evidence."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_research_9k4",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The AI correctly spotted that the sibling relationship was just a guess and routed to hypothesis-tracking. But it still narrated the relationship as if it were real (“I sent the relationship between Nora, Lois, and Elizabeth to our hypothesis tracker”), leaking the unproven premise into the user-facing reply."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_research_001",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The AI routed correctly but told the user that Patrick’s birthplace is Pennsylvania — when the project actually has Ireland as the preferred answer (from the 1850 and 1860 censuses). That’s a wrong fact handed directly to the user."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_research_001",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Completeness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The AI correctly handed off to proof-conclusion for both questions. But the user asked to identify both parents, and the AI acknowledged the mother hasn’t been found without proposing any next step to find her. Half the request was left unanswered."
    },
    {
